        {
          "name": "Generate Material - Basic (Beginner)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"topic\": \"Photosynthesis\",\n  \"level\": \"beginner\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/education/generate-material",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["api", "education", "generate-material"]
            },
            "description": "Generate educational material for beginners"
          },
          "response": [
            {
              "name": "Generate Material - Beginner Success",
              "originalRequest": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"topic\": \"Photosynthesis\",\n  \"level\": \"beginner\"\n}"
                },
                "url": {
                  "raw": "http://localhost:8000/api/education/generate-material",
                  "protocol": "http",
                  "host": ["localhost"],
                  "port": "8000",
                  "path": ["api", "education", "generate-material"]
                }
              },
              "status": "OK",
              "code": 200,
              "header": [
                {
                  "key": "content-type",
                  "value": "application/json"
                }
              ],
              "body": "{\n  \"topic\": \"Photosynthesis\",\n  \"level\": \"beginner\",\n  \"study_notes\": \"# Photosynthesis: A Beginner's Guide\\n\\n## What is Photosynthesis?\\nPhotosynthesis is the process by which plants use sunlight to make their own food. It's like a plant's kitchen where it cooks up energy from the sun!\\n\\n## Key Concepts\\n- **Sunlight**: Energy source for the process\\n- **Water**: Absorbed through roots\\n- **Carbon Dioxide**: Taken from the air\\n- **Glucose**: Sugar produced as food\\n- **Oxygen**: Released as a byproduct\\n\\n## The Simple Process\\n1. Plant leaves capture sunlight\\n2. Water from soil is transported to leaves\\n3. Carbon dioxide enters through tiny pores (stomata)\\n4. These ingredients combine to make glucose\\n5. Oxygen is released back into the air\\n\\n## Why is it Important?\\n- Plants use glucose for energy and growth\\n- Oxygen produced is essential for most life on Earth\\n- It's the foundation of most food chains\",\n  \"story_explanation\": \"Imagine a tiny factory inside a plant leaf called a chloroplast. Every sunny day, this factory opens its doors to welcome three special guests: sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide. The sunlight acts like an energetic worker, powering the entire operation. Water arrives through underground pipes (the plant's roots), and carbon dioxide floats in through tiny windows (stomata) on the leaf's surface. Inside the factory, these three ingredients are mixed together in a magical process. The sunlight provides the energy needed to combine them. After a bit of chemical magic, out comes glucose - a delicious sugar that feeds the plant and helps it grow big and strong. As a bonus, oxygen is released as a byproduct, which is perfect for us to breathe! This process happens millions of times every day in plants all around us, making it one of nature's most important factories.\",\n  \"summary\": \"Photosynthesis is the process where plants convert sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide into glucose (food) and oxygen. This process occurs in the chloroplasts of plant cells and is essential for plant growth and survival. The oxygen produced during photosynthesis is released into the atmosphere, making it vital for most life on Earth. Photosynthesis is the foundation of most food chains and ecosystems.\",\n  \"mcqs\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What is the main purpose of photosynthesis?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"To produce oxygen only\",\n        \"To convert sunlight into chemical energy (glucose)\",\n        \"To absorb water from soil\",\n        \"To release carbon dioxide\"\n      ],\n      \"correct_answer\": \"To convert sunlight into chemical energy (glucose)\",\n      \"explanation\": \"While photosynthesis does produce oxygen and absorb water, its main purpose is to convert light energy from the sun into chemical energy stored in glucose molecules, which the plant uses for growth and energy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT a requirement for photosynthesis?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Sunlight\",\n        \"Water\",\n        \"Nitrogen\",\n        \"Carbon dioxide\"\n      ],\n      \"correct_answer\": \"Nitrogen\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Photosynthesis requires sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide. While nitrogen is important for plant growth, it is not directly required for the photosynthesis process itself.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Where does photosynthesis primarily occur in plant cells?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"In the nucleus\",\n        \"In the mitochondria\",\n        \"In the chloroplasts\",\n        \"In the cell membrane\"\n      ],\n      \"correct_answer\": \"In the chloroplasts\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Photosynthesis occurs in the chloroplasts, which are specialized organelles in plant cells that contain chlorophyll and other necessary structures for the photosynthetic process.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"short_questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What are the three main inputs needed for photosynthesis?\",\n      \"expected_answer\": \"The three main inputs for photosynthesis are sunlight (light energy), water (H2O), and carbon dioxide (CO2). These are combined in the chloroplasts to produce glucose and oxygen.\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"easy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"Explain why photosynthesis is important for life on Earth.\",\n      \"expected_answer\": \"Photosynthesis is important because it produces oxygen, which most living organisms need to breathe. It also produces glucose, which serves as the primary energy source for plants and, indirectly, for all animals that eat plants or other animals. Additionally, photosynthesis forms the base of most food chains and ecosystems.\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question\": \"What happens to the glucose produced during photosynthesis?\",\n      \"expected_answer\": \"The glucose produced during photosynthesis is used by the plant for energy and growth. Some glucose is used immediately through cellular respiration to provide energy for the plant's activities. The rest is stored as starch for later use or converted into other compounds needed for plant structure and function.\",\n      \"difficulty\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"image_url\": null\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
